# Build artifacts are not version-controlled (repository policy; see the
# root AGENTS.md). `client/client.js` is rebuilt by `prepare` / `prepack`,
# which is also what puts it in the published tarball — `files` in
# package.json still lists `client`, so npm ships the built bundle without
# the repository tracking it.
#
# LEADING SLASH IS LOAD-BEARING. Without it these match a directory of that
# name at ANY depth, and `client/` silently swallows `src/client/` and
# `tests/client/` — the whole browser half and its specs — which is the
# opposite of the intent.
/node_modules/
/lib/
/client/

# Upstream's own ignores, kept as they were.
*.tgz
*.map
.DS_Store
/data/registry-snapshot.json
/data/readmes-snapshot.json
/research/
/npm-cache/

# Promotional screenshots. Kept on disk because the README and the site
# templates render them, but this repo is a private self-use fork and does not
# carry its upstream's marketing surface in version control. `files` in
# package.json lists neither `assets` nor `site`, so nothing here reaches the
# published tarball.
#
# Only the binary screenshots are ignored. `site/*.mjs` stays tracked:
# `tests/client/comments.client.spec.ts` imports `site/comments.mjs`, and
# `scripts/build-site.mjs` imports `site/locales.mjs`.
/assets/*.png
/site/assets/*.png
